\par\par \b \uc2 More Jobs Offer Flexible Hours\b0\par\par\uc2 By Austen Hufford \par \uc2 958 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 September 2022\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B1\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 It isn't just remote workers who have gained leverage over when they work.\par \par \uc2 Shift workers such as assemblers and hotel maids are also getting more flexibility to set their own hours as the pandemic and the historically tight labor market change the economy.\par \par \uc2 Manufacturers, hotels, warehouses and restaurants are allowing new hires to work just a few days a week, take on four-hour shifts or even choose new hours daily using phone apps, according to the companies, job boards and economists.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. job market has remained strong with few signs it is weakening as the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  raises interest rates to curb inflation. The unemployment rate was 3.5% in July -- matching a 50-year low -- meaning that many people have more leverage when it comes to getting jobs than before, despite an increase in layoff announcements from companies including \uc2 Ford Motor Co\uc2 ., \uc2 Walmart Inc\uc2 . and \uc2 Robinhood Markets Inc\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Over the past 12 months, 11% of postings for in-person jobs offered flexible hours, according to the online job board \uc2 ZipRecruiter\uc2 . The flexible openings typically peak in the run-up to the Christmas season as retailers and warehouses staff up. In October, 29% of job listings offered flexibility. One recent posting for a home health aide in Boston advertised weekly paychecks and custom schedules: "Choose your own hours!"\par \par \uc2 Professors at the \uc2 University of Chicago\uc2  estimated in 2020 that 37% of jobs can be done fully remotely. In-person workers can't work from home, but they can start working different hours.\par \par \uc2 "Those on-site workers need to be doing their jobs either in person or on-site," said Sinem Buber, the lead economist for \uc2 ZipRecruiter\uc2 . "They are looking for the flexibility we have as well."\par \par \uc2 While the percentage of such postings has declined in recent months, Ms. Buber said it remained above prepandemic levels, with the pullback coming from retailers. "This isn't going away," she said. "We aren't going back to 2019 when it comes to work arrangements."\par \par \uc2 The spread of flexible working hours is also being driven by workers who want part-time positions. In July, 20.7 million people were in part-time jobs of their own choosing, according to the Labor Department, while 3.9 million part-time workers said they were looking for full-time work. The proportion of the whole labor force that is choosing to work part-time hours is at its highest since early 2020.\par \par \uc2 Companies said they are offering different types of working arrangements for in-person jobs because it allows them to tap into new pools of labor and because workers are demanding it. The higher percentage of single mothers and an aging population resulting in elderly parents means that many working-age people have additional caretaking responsibilities, according to economists.\par \par \uc2 Amazon.com Inc\uc2 . said more than 100,000 of its employees have used its "Anytime Shifts" program to book their own work hours. Logistics supplier Geodis Group said more than 110,000 hours of work have been done using the company's flexible shift program on a phone app called \uc2 Shyft\uc2 . The app allows factory and manufacturing operations to function similarly to gig-economy roles like \uc2 Uber\uc2  drivers. \uc2 Geodis\uc2  posts dozens of open shifts a week, allowing workers to choose positions based on the pay rate and the hours.\par \par \uc2 Clothing retailer \uc2 Gap Inc\uc2 . has hundreds of part-time warehouse workers choosing their hours on \uc2 Shyft\uc2 . Gap and other companies say workers themselves are asking for part-time, flexible work. Many companies prefer to offer workers full-time positions.\par \par \uc2 "There's a growing population of people in which flexibility is paramount," said Kevin Releford, a logistics executive at the Gap. "You aren't going to force someone who wants maximum flexibility to work a full-time schedule."\par \par \uc2 The hotel industry views the rise of nontraditional shifts as an advantage compared with other industries because many hotels are open around the clock. "It's not a nine-to-five job," said Michael Jacobson, president of the Illinois Hotel & Lodging Association. "We have shifts starting every hour of the day."\par \par \uc2 Renee Jumper helps make washing machines two nights a week at the \uc2 GE Appliances\uc2  factory in Louisville, Ky. This schedule allows her to cook dinner for her 9-year-old daughter and take her teenage son to a studio to make music.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Jumper works every Sunday and Thursday night 10 p.m. to 6 a.m., making around $19 an hour. Typical 24-hour factory operations have three eight-hour shifts. Working two nights a week helps Ms. Jumper save money as it allows her to avoid paying for child care and to prepare meals in advance instead of going to restaurants. She is thinking about adding a third weekly shift.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Jumper doesn't get complete benefits, like health insurance, as her full-time co-workers do. She said the extra hours with her children make up for that. "It gives me more flexibility with family, to spend time with my daughter and to do meal planning and prepping," she said.\par \par \uc2 Anthony Salazar-Masias, of Ontario, Calif., uses \uc2 Amazon\uc2 's phone application to take on additional hours or switch shifts if he is busy. Mr. Salazar-Masias typically works 10-hour shifts Wednesday through Saturday on the inbound dock in a company warehouse in nearby Eastvale, Calif. He recently was able to switch his Saturday shift to a Tuesday so he could attend his nephew's 10th birthday party. He also uses the app to pick up additional overtime shifts.\par \par \uc2 "It's a really big benefit, being able to make your schedule work with whatever things you have going on in your life," he said.\par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw553\pich299\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal8295\pichgoal4485
