\par\par \b \uc2 United, Pilots Union Reopen Negotiations\b0\par\par\uc2 By Alison Sider \par \uc2 287 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 July 2022\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B2\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 United Airlines Holdings Inc\uc2 . and its pilots union will reopen contract negotiations, after pilots objected to elements of a tentative agreement the airline and the union struck last month.\par \par \uc2 United's pilots were set to wrap up voting Friday on a deal that would have included pay raises of more than 14.5% within 18 months. But United agreed to resume discussions after pilots raised concerns about aspects of the deal, the \uc2 Air Line Pilots Association\uc2 's United chapter told members in a message Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The delay underscores the difficulty of such negotiations after two years of the Covid-19 pandemic and the upheaval it caused for airline employees. Big airlines are replacing thousands of pilots who retired or left during the pandemic, creating staffing pressures for smaller airlines that have been facing a shortage of pilots. Pilots at some other airlines have been seeking improvements to scheduling practices and other quality-of-life issues, due to what they have described as exhausting schedules.\par \par \uc2 "The bargaining environment shifts rapidly, and we will use this opportunity to address your concerns," Capt. Mike Hamilton, chairman of the United Master Executive Council, wrote to pilots.\par \par \uc2 United's union plans to survey pilots about their concerns, and the vote could be delayed by up to three months, it said. Objections so far have largely been related to work rules, a union spokesman said.\par \par \uc2 United declined to comment.\par \par \uc2 Postponing the vote is a setback for United, which was the first major U.S. carrier to strike a tentative deal with its pilots. Its agreement was also expected to serve as a reference point for other airlines and pilot unions that are currently in talks.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020220714ei7e0001r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
