\par\par \b \uc2 Business News: Atlantic City Casino Workers Reach Pacts With \uc2 MGM\uc2 , Caesars\b0\par\par\uc2 By Katherine Sayre \par \uc2 272 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 July 2022\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B6\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Atlantic City casino union workers reached tentative agreements with \uc2 MGM Resorts International\uc2  and \uc2 Caesars Entertainment Inc\uc2 . to avoid a Fourth of July weekend strike, according to the union.\par \par \uc2 Unite Here\uc2  Local 54 union organizers, who have been seeking pay raises, said the agreements would avoid strikes at \uc2 MGM Resorts\uc2 ' Borgata casino and \uc2 Caesars Entertainment\uc2 's Caesars, Harrah's and Tropicana properties. The union had voted to authorize a possible strike Friday without a deal. The casinos employ about 4,500 unionized workers, according to Local 54.\par \par \uc2 The union declined to provide details about the agreements. The members must approve the deals before they are final, a union spokeswoman said. The casino companies didn't comment on the deals' terms.\par \par \uc2 Local 54 organizers have said wages have fallen behind in recent years, and workers deserve raises now that casinos have bounced back from the pandemic. Workers at five of the city's nine casinos had voted to authorize the union's negotiating committee to call strikes beginning Friday without an agreement.\par \par \uc2 The union also set a strike deadline of Sunday for the Hard Rock casino. A union spokeswoman said negotiations will continue with Hard Rock representatives.\par \par \uc2 Atlantic City casino revenue this year, through May, has surpassed prepandemic levels in 2019. From January through May, casinos reported $1.08 billion in slot-machine and table-game revenue this year, compared with nearly $1.03 billion over the same period in 2019, according to New Jersey gambling regulators. The companies have also seen recordgambling revenue in Las Vegas, Nevada gambling regulators say.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020220701ei7100028\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
