\par\par \b \uc2 Business News: Atlantic City Casino Workers Vote Strike\b0\par\par\uc2 By Katherine Sayre \par \uc2 273 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 June 2022\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B6\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Atlantic City casino workers voted to authorize a strike for increased wages ahead of the Fourth of July weekend.\par \par \uc2 Unite Here\uc2  Local 54's contracts with Atlantic City's major casino-hotels -- including \uc2 MGM Resorts International\uc2 's Borgata and \uc2 Caesars Entertainment Inc\uc2 .'s Harrah's and Caesars properties -- expired May 31. Organizers say wages have fallen behind in recent years through the 2008 economic downturn, the damages from Hurricane Sandy in 2012, the pandemic and inflation.\par \par \uc2 A Caesars spokeswoman declined to comment. \uc2 MGM Resorts\uc2  didn't comment.\par \par \uc2 Ruthann Joyce, a bartender at Harrah's who has worked in the industry since 1980, said the rising costs of groceries, gasoline and rent are putting pressure on workers with no end in sight. Meanwhile, the casino industry is rebounding following the pandemic closures. "We haven't had any raises, and now is the time -- when the companies are doing well -- to address that," Ms. Joyce said.\par \par \uc2 Workers voted by 96% to authorize the union's negotiating committee to call a strike at five of the city's nine casinos, including the Borgata, Harrah's, Caesars, Tropicana and the Hard Rock. Those properties include 6,000 workers. Local 54 in total represents more than 10,000 casino service workers, including housekeepers, bartenders, cooks, cocktail servers and doormen.\par \par \uc2 The union set a deadline of July 1 for Borgata, Harrah's, Caesars and Tropicana followed by a July 3 deadline at the Hard Rock.\par \par \uc2 Two casinos, Ocean and \uc2 Bally\uc2 's, have agreed to follow any deal the union reaches with the other properties, a union spokeswoman said.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020220616ei6g00025\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
