\par\par \uc2 Technology\par \b \uc2 Raytheon\uc2  to Move Its Base Closer To Pentagon, Joining Defense Peers\b0\par\par\uc2 By Doug Cameron \par \uc2 380 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 June 2022\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B4\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Raytheon Technologies Corp\uc2 . said it would move its global headquarters to the Washington, D.C., area later this year, joining other big aerospace and defense contractors seeking more proximity to the Pentagon, regulators and lawmakers.\par \par \uc2 The world's second-largest defense company by sales said it plans to use an existing facility in the Rosslyn neighborhood of Arlington in northern Virginia as its corporate head office from the third quarter of this year. The company's current headquarters are in Waltham, Mass.\par \par \uc2 Raytheon\uc2  said it remains committed to the mix of hybrid and remote work it developed during the Covid-19 pandemic that at one point involved more than half of its 174,000 employees working from home. While more are now back in the office, the company has created campuses at some facilities for hot-desking and is reducing its office real estate footprint by one-fifth.\par \par \uc2 "The company has proven the effectiveness of a remote or hybrid working model, with employees working where they need to be to perform at an optimal level," said a \uc2 Raytheon\uc2  spokesman.\par \par \uc2 Raytheon\uc2  said it plans to retain its existing facility in Waltham, which became the company's global headquarters following its creation through the merger of \uc2 Raytheon Co\uc2 . and \uc2 United Technologies Corp\uc2 . in April 2020.\par \par \uc2 The maker of \uc2 Pratt & Whitney\uc2  engines and Patriot missile-defense systems joins most of the major U.S. aerospace and defense companies in basing in the D.C. area.\par \par \uc2 Boeing Co\uc2 . last month announced plans to move its global headquarters to Arlington, where its defense leadership is already based. \uc2 Lockheed Martin Corp\uc2 ., \uc2 Northrop Grumman Corp\uc2 ., \uc2 General Dynamics Corp\uc2 . and big defense services players such as \uc2 CACI International Inc\uc2 . are also based in the D.C. region.\par \par \uc2 L3Harris Technologies Inc\uc2 . is one outlier, based in Melbourne, Fla.\par \par \uc2 The sector's concentration in northern Virginia has put defense companies into fierce competition for workers, especially in software and data engineering. \uc2 Amazon.com Inc\uc2 . is developing one of its satellite headquarters in Arlington.\par \par \uc2 Some defense companies, including Reston, Va.-based \uc2 Leidos Holdings Inc\uc2 ., have responded by shifting more work outside the area to locales such as St. Louis that also host large government and defense facilities.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020220608ei680000z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
